nderstanding:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">ETag vs Last-Modified gi=E1=BB=
=91ng nh=C6=B0 different verification methods:</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Last-Modified</strong> =
=3D timestamp on document</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">"Has this document been touched=
 since I last saw it?"</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Simple but imprecise (1-second =
granularity)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Can give false positives (file =
touched but content unchanged)</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>ETag</strong> =3D conten=
t fingerprint</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">"Is the content exactly the sam=
e as what I have?"</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Precise but requires computatio=
n</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Strong ETag: byte-level accurac=
y</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Weak ETag: semantic equivalence=
</li>
</ul>
