<h4 class=3D"text-base font-bold text-text-100 mt-1">=F0=9F=93=96 HTTPS Upg=
rade Redirects - Security Meets Performance</h4>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>=F0=9F=8C=B1 Ngu=E1=BB=
=93n G=E1=BB=91c &amp; Motivation:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">HTTPS upgrade redirects represen=
t critical intersection c=E1=BB=A7a security v=C3=A0 performance optimizati=
on. Modern web applications must handle HTTP-to-HTTPS upgrades efficiently =
while maintaining optimal user experience.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Evolution timeline:</str=
ong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>2010s:</strong> Manual =
HTTPS implementation</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>2014:</strong> Let's En=
crypt democratizes SSL certificates</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>2016:</strong> HTTP/2 r=
equires HTTPS for most benefits</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>2018:</strong> Chrome m=
arks HTTP sites as "Not Secure"</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>2020s:</strong> HTTPS-f=
irst policies, automatic upgrades</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>System Architect perspec=
tive:</strong> HTTPS redirects affect caching strategies, CDN configuration=
s, and overall application architecture decisions.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>=F0=9F=94=AC B=E1=BA=A3n=
 Ch=E1=BA=A5t &amp; Mechanism:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>HTTPS Upgrade Strategy I=
